{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artin rees lemma artin rees lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","fileName":"Artin-Rees Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artin-Rees Lemma","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:10\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Graded Algebra and Hilbert Theory]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Graded Algebra and Hilbert Theory","Krull Intersection Theorem","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artin rees lemma artin rees lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","fileName":"Artin-Rees Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artin-Rees Lemma","heading":"Artin-Rees Lemma","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Let I be an ideal in a Noetherian ring, M a finitely generated module, and N a submodule. The Artin-Rees lemma says that for some k, IⁿM ∩ N = Iⁿ⁻ᵏ(IᵏM ∩ N) for all n ≥ k.\n\nThus the filtration induced on N eventually follows a fixed rule. The result controls intersections with ideal powers and supports [[Krull Intersection Theorem|Krull's intersection theorem]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Graded Algebra and Hilbert Theory","Krull Intersection Theorem","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"artin rees lemma artin rees lemma","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Artin-Rees Lemma.md","fileName":"Artin-Rees Lemma.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Artin-Rees Lemma","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Graded Algebra and Hilbert Theory","Krull Intersection Theorem","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}